                <section id="about">
                  <p>Hello stranger. Welcome to my corner of the internet.</p>
                  <p>Carl Sagan once said "We are a way for the cosmos to know itself." My goal is to build machines that can understand the cosmos, and deepen our own understanding along the way. Right now I spend most of my time on low-level programming. Eventually I want to go further down the stack, into the electrical, mechanical, and materials engineering that make modern hardware work.</p>
                  <p>I believe that if I cannot build something, I don't really understand it. That's why, if you know me IRL, you'll find me reversing things and writing my own implementations constantly.</p>
                  <p>See <a href="/posts/">posts</a> for my writing.</p>
                </section>
